{"id":"pictures-of-the-floating-world","title":"Pictures of the Floating World","author":"Amy Lowell","year":"1919","note":"Imagist flashes and Japanese-inflected miniatures — how little language tilts a room.","minutes":456,"cover":"","coverAlt":"","scenes":[{"id":"s0","title":"Streets","place":"Streets","reentry":"(Adapted from the poet Yakura Sangin, 1769)","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s1","title":"In Autumn","place":"In Autumn","reentry":"OnE night","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s2","title":"Circumstance","place":"Circumstance","reentry":"Upon the maple leaves","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s3","title":"Angles","place":"Angles","reentry":"THE rain is dark against the white sky,","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s4","title":"VicaRIOUS","place":"VicaRIOUS","reentry":"WueEn I stand under the willow-tree","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s5","title":"Negar Kioto","place":"Negar Kioto","reentry":"As I crossed over the bridge of Ariwarano Narikira,","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s6","title":"Desolation","place":"Desolation","reentry":"Unpver the plum-blossoms are nightingales ;","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s7","title":"YosHIwaRA LAMENT","place":"YosHIwaRA LAMENT","reentry":"GOLDEN peacocks","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s8","title":"Sunshine","place":"Sunshine","reentry":"THE pool is edged with the blade-like leaves of irises.","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s9","title":"Pictures of the Floating World 7","place":"Pictures of the Floating World 7","reentry":"It suddenly stiffens","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s10","title":"Illusion","place":"Illusion","reentry":"WALKING beside the tree-peonies,","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s11","title":"A YxEAR PassEs","place":"A YxEAR PassEs","reentry":"Bryonp the porcelain fence of the pleasure garden,","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s12","title":"A Lover","place":"A Lover","reentry":"Ir I could catch the green lantern of the firefly","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s13","title":"To a Huspanp","place":"To a Huspanp","reentry":"BricuHTer than fireflies upon the Uji River","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s14","title":"Tue FisHERMAN’s WIFE","place":"Tue FisHERMAN’s WIFE","reentry":"WuHENn I am alone,","prompt":"What image stays?"},{"id":"s15","title":"From CHINA","place":"From CHINA","reentry":"I rHouGutT: —","prompt":"What image stays?"}],"breaths":[{"id":"s0-0","sceneId":"s0","text":"(Adapted from the poet Yakura Sangin, 1769)"},{"id":"s0-1","sceneId":"s0","text":"As I wandered through the eight hundred and eight"},{"id":"s0-2","sceneId":"s0","text":"streets of the city,"},{"id":"s0-3","sceneId":"s0","text":"I saw nothing so beautiful"},{"id":"s0-4","sceneId":"s0","text":"As the Women of the Green Houses,"},{"id":"s0-5","sceneId":"s0","text":"With their girdles of spun gold,"},{"id":"s0-6","sceneId":"s0","text":"And their long-sleeved dresses,"},{"id":"s0-7","sceneId":"s0","text":"Coloured like the graining of wood."},{"id":"s0-8","sceneId":"s0","text":"As they walk,"},{"id":"s0-9","sceneId":"s0","text":"The hemsof their outer garments flutter open,"},{"id":"s0-10","sceneId":"s0","text":"And the blood-red linings glow like sharp-toothed"},{"id":"s0-11","sceneId":"s0","text":"maple leaves"},{"id":"s1-0","sceneId":"s1","text":"In Autumn."},{"id":"s1-1","sceneId":"s1","text":"By MEssENGER"},{"id":"s1-2","sceneId":"s1","text":"OnE night"},{"id":"s1-3","sceneId":"s1","text":"When there was a clear moon,"},{"id":"s1-4","sceneId":"s1","text":"I sat down"},{"id":"s1-5","sceneId":"s1","text":"To write a poem"},{"id":"s1-6","sceneId":"s1","text":"About maple-trees."},{"id":"s1-7","sceneId":"s1","text":"But the dazzle of moonlight"},{"id":"s1-8","sceneId":"s1","text":"In the ink"},{"id":"s1-9","sceneId":"s1","text":"Blinded me,"},{"id":"s1-10","sceneId":"s1","text":"And I could only write"},{"id":"s1-11","sceneId":"s1","text":"What I remembered."},{"id":"s1-12","sceneId":"s1","text":"Therefore, on the wrapping of my poem"},{"id":"s1-13","sceneId":"s1","text":"I have inscribed your name."},{"id":"s2-0","sceneId":"s2","text":"Upon the maple leaves"},{"id":"s2-1","sceneId":"s2","text":"The dew shines red,"},{"id":"s2-2","sceneId":"s2","text":"But on the lotus blossom"},{"id":"s2-3","sceneId":"s2","text":"It has the pale transparence of tears."},{"id":"s3-0","sceneId":"s3","text":"THE rain is dark against the white sky,"},{"id":"s3-1","sceneId":"s3","text":"Or white against the foliage of eucalyptus-trees."},{"id":"s3-2","sceneId":"s3","text":"But, in the cistern, it is a sheet of mauve and amber,"},{"id":"s3-3","sceneId":"s3","text":"Because of the chrysanthemums"},{"id":"s3-4","sceneId":"s3","text":"Heaped about its edge."},{"id":"s4-0","sceneId":"s4","text":"WueEn I stand under the willow-tree"},{"id":"s4-1","sceneId":"s4","text":"Above the river,"},{"id":"s4-2","sceneId":"s4","text":"In my straw-coloured silken garment"},{"id":"s4-3","sceneId":"s4","text":"Embroidered with purple chrysanthemums,            ,"},{"id":"s4-4","sceneId":"s4","text":"It is not at the bright water"},{"id":"s4-5","sceneId":"s4","text":"That I am gazing,"},{"id":"s4-6","sceneId":"s4","text":"But at your portrait,"},{"id":"s4-7","sceneId":"s4","text":"Which I have caused to be painted"},{"id":"s4-8","sceneId":"s4","text":"On my fan."},{"id":"s5-0","sceneId":"s5","text":"As I crossed over the bridge of Ariwarano Narikira,"},{"id":"s5-1","sceneId":"s5","text":"I saw that the waters were purple"},{"id":"s5-2","sceneId":"s5","text":"With the floating leaves of maples."},{"id":"s6-0","sceneId":"s6","text":"Unpver the plum-blossoms are nightingales ;"},{"id":"s6-1","sceneId":"s6","text":"But the sea is hidden in an egg-white mist,"},{"id":"s6-2","sceneId":"s6","text":"And they are silent."},{"id":"s7-0","sceneId":"s7","text":"GOLDEN peacocks"},{"id":"s7-1","sceneId":"s7","text":"Under blossoming cherry-trees,"},{"id":"s7-2","sceneId":"s7","text":"But on all the wide sea"},{"id":"s7-3","sceneId":"s7","text":"There is no boat."},{"id":"s8-0","sceneId":"s8","text":"THE pool is edged with the blade-like leaves of irises."},{"id":"s8-1","sceneId":"s8","text":"If I throw a stone into the placid water,"},{"id":"s9-0","sceneId":"s9","text":"It suddenly stiffens"},{"id":"s9-1","sceneId":"s9","text":"Into rings and rings"},{"id":"s9-2","sceneId":"s9","text":"Of sharp gold wire."},{"id":"s10-0","sceneId":"s10","text":"WALKING beside the tree-peonies,"},{"id":"s10-1","sceneId":"s10","text":"I saw a beetle"},{"id":"s10-2","sceneId":"s10","text":"Whose wings were of black lacquer spotted with milk."},{"id":"s10-3","sceneId":"s10","text":"I would have caught it,"},{"id":"s10-4","sceneId":"s10","text":"But it ran from me swiftly"},{"id":"s10-5","sceneId":"s10","text":"And hid under the stone lotus"},{"id":"s10-6","sceneId":"s10","text":"Which supports the statue of Buddha."},{"id":"s11-0","sceneId":"s11","text":"Bryonp the porcelain fence of the pleasure garden,"},{"id":"s11-1","sceneId":"s11","text":"I hear the frogs in the blue-green rice-fields;   |"},{"id":"s11-2","sceneId":"s11","text":"But the sword-shaped moon"},{"id":"s11-3","sceneId":"s11","text":"Has cut my heart in two."},{"id":"s12-0","sceneId":"s12","text":"Ir I could catch the green lantern of the firefly"},{"id":"s12-1","sceneId":"s12","text":"I could see to write you a letter."},{"id":"s13-0","sceneId":"s13","text":"BricuHTer than fireflies upon the Uji River"},{"id":"s13-1","sceneId":"s13","text":"Are your words in the dark, Beloved."},{"id":"s14-0","sceneId":"s14","text":"WuHENn I am alone,"},{"id":"s14-1","sceneId":"s14","text":"The wind in the pine-trees"},{"id":"s14-2","sceneId":"s14","text":"Is like the shuffling of waves"},{"id":"s14-3","sceneId":"s14","text":"Upon the wooden sides of a boat."},{"id":"s15-0","sceneId":"s15","text":"I rHouGutT: —"}]}